Migration Runbook – Cutover & Rollback (Go OR No‑Go)

1. Pre Cutover Checklist
•	Validate source volumes (ownership, ACLs, export policies).
•	 Confirm bandwidth availability (10 Gbps off hours preferred).
•	 Ensure CMDB entries are up to date for target volumes.
•	 Dry run migration wave with hash sampling for integrity.
•	 Approval gates signed off in ServiceNow (especially for GxP datasets).

2. Cutover Procedure
1.	Freeze writes on source volumes (application downtime window).
2.	Final SnapMirror sync or file level delta transfer.
3.	Switch DNS/DFS mappings to target cluster.
4.	Validate access from representative clients (SMB/NFS).
5.	Enable monitoring (latency, error rates, throughput).
6.	Update CMDB with new ownership and location.
7.	Notify stakeholders of cutover completion.

3. Go/No Go Criteria
•	Data integrity checks pass (hash sample ≥ 99.9% match).
•	Latency within SLA (< 5 ms for Tier 1 workloads).
•	No critical errors in logs during validation.
•	GxP evidence collected and stored.
•	Abort if any of the above fail.

4. Rollback Procedure
1.	Revert DNS/DFS mappings to source cluster.
2.	Re enable writes on source volumes.
3.	Restore snapshot taken pre cutover.
4.	Notify stakeholders of rollback execution.
5.	Log incident in ServiceNow with evidence.
6.	Schedule re attempt after root cause analysis.

5. Post Cutover Actions
•	Monitor workloads for 24 hours.
•	Collect performance metrics and compare against baseline.
•	Confirm CMDB entries reflect new state.
•	Archive migration logs and evidence for compliance.
•	Close migration wave in ServiceNow.

